WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.699
Film Courage: Forgive my naïveté, but why
does name talent not want to do [be in] horror

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:04.699
[movies]?

00:00:04.699 --> 00:00:05.880
Is the budget too low or is there a stigma
attached?

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:10.810
Mark Heidelberger, Producer: I think named
talent is probably more adverse to horror

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.840
because of a stigma.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.260
I don’t think it has to do with…because
some horror pictures have decent budgets and

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:20.960
I mean you could be going after maybe the
same names I’d be going after if it was

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.580
a romance or comedy on that same budget level.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.380
So I don’t think it’s the money.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.980
I do think it’s more the stigma.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.939
My horror picture I had several casting directors
pass.

00:00:31.939 --> 00:00:38.300
We had trouble finding a casting…we were
willing to pay them a decent salary and a

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.899
lot of them just didn’t want to take it
and I think because they felt like it was

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:50.899
going to be tough to get even a modest names
on board a horror movie…you know it’s

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:56.650
not like SE7EN where it’s like this smart
thriller with some kind of really pseudo horroresque

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:02.610
elements, it’s like straight horror, it’s
a tough sell and I think a lot of actors don’t

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.869
feel like maybe if they’re already established
that they need to do that genre, that it’s

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:12.979
going to help elevate their career, they want
to do more serious work or whatever that might

00:01:12.979 --> 00:01:13.979
be.

00:01:13.979 --> 00:01:15.810
I’m not saying I agree with that.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.280
I think our picture THE BASEMENT I thought
had a really, unique interesting storyline.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.459
Very psychological or it had some gruesome
moments but I think those gruesome moments

00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:29.159
were enough to sort of scare people away.

00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:34.100
So I think that stigma could be the managers
telling them look you don’t want to do horror

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.169
because the stigma is not real, perception
is reality.

00:01:38.169 --> 00:01:41.849
So if it’s perceived enough to be there
then they’re just like better steer clear,

00:01:41.849 --> 00:01:48.770
you’re getting offers on these other dramas,
romantic comedies, action pictures do those

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:51.819
because there is no stigma with those so go
ahead (they are safe).

00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:57.599
That’s my assessment and if that’s a 100%
accurate but from what I’ve seen that’s

00:01:57.599 --> 00:02:04.119
definitely actors avoiding horror pictures
outside of big studio ones are definitely

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:07.770
real because I’ve experience it firsthand
but that would be my assessment on why.

